<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Treasury sees gradual easing from Dec 96 qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ Treasury sees gradual easing from Dec 96 qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury said on Thursday that signs of abating inflationary pressures would allow New Zealand monetary conditions to ease gradually from the December 1996 quarter.</p>
<p>However, it said monetary conditions were expected to remain &quot;relatively firm&quot; as a pick-up in activity in 1997/98 was expected to add to inflation pressures.</p>
<p>&quot;Monetary conditions are expected to begin easing from the December 1996 quarter,&quot; Treasury said.</p>
</text>
